    ],
    "correct_answer": "D",
    "explanation": "Equal area gives ds^2=Do^2-Di^2. Hence J ratio=(Do^2+Di^2)/(Do^2-Di^2)=(4+1)/(4-1)=5/3."
  },
  {
    "display_order": 134,
    "question_text": "[Structural Analysis] Two axle loads, 60 and 40 kN, are 2 m apart on an 8 m simply supported beam. The largest possible left reaction, allowing an axle at the support, is:",
    "options": [
      {
        "value": "A",
        "text": "75 kN"
      },
      {
        "value": "B",
        "text": "85 kN"
      },
      {
        "value": "C",
        "text": "100 kN"
      },
      {
        "value": "D",
        "text": "90 kN"
      }
    ],
    "correct_answer": "D",
    "explanation": "Place 60 kN at the left support and 40 kN 2 m inside. RA=60+40(6/8)=90 kN; reversing axles gives 85 kN."
  },
  {
    "display_order": 135,
    "question_text": "[Structural Analysis] A portal frame is geometrically symmetric with equal columns but carries an asymmetric horizontal load. Which statement is justified?",
    "options": [
      {
        "value": "A",
        "text": "Axial forces alone can always resist the load"
      },
      {
        "value": "B",
        "text": "Every beam end moment is zero"
      },
      {
        "value": "C",
        "text": "Symmetric geometry alone prohibits sway"
      },
      {
        "value": "D",
        "text": "A sway degree of freedom generally remains necessary"
      }
    ],
    "correct_answer": "D",
    "explanation": "Loading as well as geometry determines sway. A lateral load generally excites frame translation."
  },
  {
    "display_order": 136,
    "question_text": "[Steel Structures & Prestressed Concrete] A straight 20 m tendon undergoes anchorage slip 4 mm. With Ep=200 GPa and uniform slip-induced strain reduction, stress loss is:",
    "options": [
      {
        "value": "A",
        "text": "4 MPa"
      },
      {
        "value": "B",
        "text": "80 MPa"
      },
      {
        "value": "C",
        "text": "20 MPa"
      },
      {
        "value": "D",
        "text": "40 MPa"
      }
    ],
    "correct_answer": "D",
    "explanation": "Loss=Ep delta/L=200000x4/20000=40 MPa. Uniform loss is the stated idealization."
  },
  {
    "display_order": 137,
    "question_text": "[Strength of Materials] A 1 kN weight falls 20 mm before stretching a vertical elastic bar whose static extension under that weight is 2 mm. Neglect bar mass. Maximum force is approximately:",
    "options": [
      {
        "value": "A",
        "text": "10 kN"
      },
      {
        "value": "B",
        "text": "3.32 kN"
      },
      {
        "value": "C",
        "text": "2 kN"
      },
      {
        "value": "D",
        "text": "5.58 kN"
      }
    ],
    "correct_answer": "D",
    "explanation": "Energy balance gives P/W=1+sqrt(1+2h/delta_static)=1+sqrt(21)=5.58."
  },
  {
    "display_order": 138,
    "question_text": "[Transportation Engineering] A vehicle enters a circular curve through a transition where curvature grows linearly with distance. At constant speed, lateral acceleration through the transition is:",
    "options": [
      {
        "value": "A",
        "text": "Constant from the first transition point"
      },
      {
        "value": "B",
        "text": "Linear in distance, giving constant rate of change with time"
