      {
        "value": "C",
        "text": "Inverse to distance"
      },
      {
        "value": "D",
        "text": "Zero until the circular arc begins"
      }
    ],
    "correct_answer": "B",
    "explanation": "Lateral acceleration is v^2 times curvature. Linear curvature and constant speed produce a constant time rate of lateral acceleration."
  },
  {
    "display_order": 139,
    "question_text": "[RCC Design] A doubly reinforced beam needs an additional moment of 80 kNm beyond its concrete-limited component. If compression steel design stress is 350 MPa and the steel couple arm is 400 mm, required compression-steel area is:",
    "options": [
      {
        "value": "A",
        "text": "228.6 mm^2"
      },
      {
        "value": "B",
        "text": "800 mm^2"
