    "correct_answer": "B",
    "explanation": "NPSHa=10.3-0.3-4-1=5.0 m relative to the pump suction reference."
  },
  {
    "display_order": 142,
    "question_text": "[Strength of Materials] A transverse load acts through the centroid of an open channel section. Why may the beam still twist?",
    "options": [
      {
        "value": "A",
        "text": "Every centroidal load necessarily creates an axial force"
      },
      {
        "value": "B",
        "text": "The centroid generally differs from the shear centre"
      },
      {
        "value": "C",
        "text": "The shear centre must lie on every flange edge"
      },
      {
        "value": "D",
        "text": "Open sections have zero torsional rigidity"
      }
    ],
    "correct_answer": "B",
    "explanation": "Bending without twist requires the transverse force to pass through the shear centre, which need not coincide with the centroid."
  },
  {
    "display_order": 143,
    "question_text": "[Steel Structures & Prestressed Concrete] Two 200 mm effective-length fillet welds have size 6 mm. Taking throat 0.7s and allowable shear 100 MPa, total direct-load capacity is:",
    "options": [
      {
        "value": "A",
        "text": "84 kN"
      },
      {
        "value": "B",
        "text": "240 kN"
      },
      {
        "value": "C",
        "text": "336 kN"
      },
      {
        "value": "D",
        "text": "168 kN"
      }
    ],
    "correct_answer": "D",
    "explanation": "Throat area=2x200x0.7x6=1680 mm^2. Capacity=1680x100=168000 N."
  },
  {
    "display_order": 144,
    "question_text": "[Structural Analysis] For two truss members, N=[30,-20] kN under real loading, n=[0.5,-0.25] under a unit load, and L/AE=0.02 mm/kN for each. Displacement in the unit-load direction is:",
    "options": [
      {
        "value": "A",
        "text": "0.40 mm"
      },
      {
        "value": "B",
        "text": "0.10 mm"
      },
      {
        "value": "C",
        "text": "0.20 mm"
      },
      {
        "value": "D",
        "text": "0.80 mm"
      }
    ],
    "correct_answer": "A",
    "explanation": "Virtual work gives sum(N n L/AE)=(15+5)(0.02)=0.40 mm; compression signs must be retained."
  },
  {
    "display_order": 145,
    "question_text": "[Surveying] For horizontal tacheometry D=Ks with K=100 exact, independent upper and lower staff readings each have standard error 1 mm. Standard error of D is approximately:",
    "options": [
      {
        "value": "A",
        "text": "0.141 m"
      },
      {
        "value": "B",
        "text": "0.200 m"
      },
      {
        "value": "C",
        "text": "0.100 m"
      },
      {
        "value": "D",
        "text": "0.071 m"
      }
    ],
    "correct_answer": "A",
    "explanation": "Intercept standard error=sqrt(1^2+1^2) mm. Multiplying by 100 gives 141.4 mm or 0.141 m."
  },
  {
    "display_order": 146,
    "question_text": "[Transportation Engineering] A flexible pavement has bottom-up repeated-load cracking but little permanent wheel-path depression. Which distress mechanism is most consistent?",
    "options": [
      {
        "value": "A",
        "text": "Fatigue from repeated tensile strain"
      },
      {
        "value": "B",
        "text": "Pure thermal expansion without stress"
      },
      {
        "value": "C",
        "text": "Loss of road camber alone"
      },
      {
        "value": "D",
        "text": "Rutting as the only mechanism"
      }
    ],
    "correct_answer": "A",
    "explanation": "Bottom-up fatigue is linked to repeated tensile strain near the bituminous-layer bottom; rutting is permanent deformation."
  },
  {
    "display_order": 147,
    "question_text": "[Environmental Engineering] Why is uncontrolled air entry undesirable in a methane-producing anaerobic digester?",
    "options": [
      {
        "value": "A",
        "text": "It converts every gas molecule to nitrogen"
      },
      {
        "value": "B",
        "text": "It necessarily doubles methane yield"
      },
      {
        "value": "C",
        "text": "Methanogens require high dissolved oxygen"
      },
      {
        "value": "D",
        "text": "It disrupts anaerobic operation and can create a flammable gas mixture"
      }
    ],
    "correct_answer": "D",
    "explanation": "Methanogenesis requires anaerobic conditions; mixing air with biogas can introduce combustion hazards as well as process disturbance."
  },
  {
    "display_order": 148,
    "question_text": "[Strength of Materials] A solid rectangular shaft twists elastically. Which circular-shaft assumption fails?",
    "options": [
      {
        "value": "A",
        "text": "Torque must satisfy equilibrium"
      },
      {
        "value": "B",
        "text": "Stress remains proportional to torque in linear elasticity"
