    "correct_answer": "D",
    "explanation": "Noncircular sections generally warp. The circular formula tau=Tr/J cannot be transferred unchanged to rectangles."
  },
  {
    "display_order": 149,
    "question_text": "[Hydrology & Irrigation Engineering] A double-mass curve changes slope from 1.20 in the reliable period to 0.90 in the inconsistent period. To adjust an inconsistent recorded annual total of 600 mm to the reliable regime, use:",
    "options": [
      {
        "value": "A",
        "text": "675 mm"
      },
      {
        "value": "B",
        "text": "600 mm"
      },
      {
        "value": "C",
        "text": "800 mm"
      },
      {
        "value": "D",
        "text": "450 mm"
      }
    ],
    "correct_answer": "C",
    "explanation": "Correction factor is reliable slope/inconsistent slope=1.20/0.90. Adjusted rainfall=600x4/3=800 mm."
  },
  {
    "display_order": 150,
    "question_text": "[RCC Design] For this problem adopt e_min=L/500+D/30, but not less than 20 mm. A column has unsupported length 4000 mm and depth 600 mm. Required minimum eccentricity is:",
    "options": [
      {
        "value": "A",
        "text": "8 mm"
      },
      {
        "value": "B",
        "text": "28 mm"
